    "created_at": "2024-11-27T15:46:49Z",
    "updated_at": "2024-11-27T15:46:49Z",
    "body": "The spec allows [aborting parsing for any parse error](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#parse-errors), and a parse error is needed to trigger this condition.\r\n\r\nThe spec also allows [implementation-defined limits to guard against DoS attacks](https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#algorithm-limits).\r\n\r\nSince browsers can be DoS'd in various ways, adding limits to the HTML parser for reconstructing formatting elements doesn't seem so attractive vs web compat risk.",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
